MODULE processing_sql
PURPOSE Inspect AFC table schemas, combine approved source tables, and prepare date-range extracts.
PAPER Section 5.1.1 data periods; Section 4.2.1 event-time observability.

PROCEDURE main
    INPUT script options and externally supplied database profile.
    OUTPUT extraction receipts, schema report, and split manifest.
    VALIDATE that selected modes have complete nonempty settings.
    VALIDATE identifiers against the configured database/schema namespace.
    REQUIRE every destination differs from every protected source table.
    PARSE date bounds under date_semantics.
    REQUIRE end date is not earlier than start date.
    INITIALIZE connection and cursor handles as unopened.
    TRY:
        OPEN one connection using the external credential profile.
        OPEN a cursor.
        REPORT connection success without printing the connection object or secret.
        READ source table schema metadata.
        REPORT column names, data types, and date-field definitions.
        VERIFY required journey and timestamp columns.
        REQUIRE entry_time, origin code, exit_time, and destination code for full observability.
        IF only aggregate final OD counts are available:
            FLAG the source as insufficient for finished/unfinished reconstruction.
        END IF
        READ a bounded set of distinct service dates for schema validation.
        REPORT date range and count without publishing raw journey rows.
        IF combined_table is enabled:
            REQUIRE at least one approved source table.
            VERIFY source columns have compatible meanings and units.
            VERIFY timestamp precision and station-code domains are compatible.
            CREATE a staging destination using the declared schema.
            FOR EACH approved source table:
                COPY the declared canonical columns into staging.
                RETAIN source-table provenance where required.
            END FOR
            APPLY the declared duplicate-journey policy across source tables.

            VERIFY output row counts and timestamp bounds.
            PUBLISH staging as combined_table_name under destination_policy.
            RECORD the union source list and deduplication diagnostics.
        END IF
        IF date_filter_need is enabled:
            FOR EACH requested service date d:
                DERIVE the intended destination name using validated date formatting.
                CALL extract_filtered_data for the single-date range [d,d].
                RECORD the returned extraction receipt.
            END FOR
        END IF
        IF date_filter_and_combine is enabled:
            REQUIRE the range_jobs list contains actual configured jobs.
            FOR EACH job in range_jobs:
                CALL extract_filtered_data with that job's source and bounds.
                STORE its declared role: training, validation, test, or history support.
                RECORD the returned extraction receipt.
            END FOR
        END IF
        VERIFY training, validation, and test target intervals are disjoint.
        VERIFY target-period boundaries match the requested published-study setting.
        STORE the split manifest and extraction diagnostics.
    ON database or validation error:
        ROLLBACK transactional changes where supported.
        MARK any nontransactional staging outputs incomplete.
        REPORT the failed stage without exposing query credentials or passenger identifiers.

    FINALLY:
        CLOSE cursor if it was opened.
        CLOSE connection if it was opened.
    END TRY
    RETURN completed receipts and any failure statuses.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE extract_filtered_data
    INPUT cursor, conn, source_table_name, new_table_name, start_date, end_date.
    INPUT column_contract, date_semantics, destination_policy.
    OUTPUT extraction receipt and validation report.
    CHECK source and destination identifiers are nonempty and distinct.
    VERIFY both belong to the intended database scope.
    VERIFY the source exists and has the required canonical columns.
    PARSE the supplied date bounds.
    TRANSLATE inclusive service-date bounds into an explicit timestamp selection.
    IF the source field is a date:
        SELECT dates from start_date through end_date inclusively.
    ELSE IF the source field is a timestamp:
        USE an equivalent start-inclusive, next-boundary-exclusive interval.
        RESPECT the service timezone and any declared service-day rollover.
    END IF
    BIND date values as query parameters.
    RESOLVE table identifiers from validated configuration, not arbitrary date text.
    CREATE an empty staging table using the required source schema.
    SELECT canonical journey fields within the requested entry-cohort date range.
    PRESERVE exit events required to resolve those entry cohorts.
    KEEP eventual exits after the entry-date range when completing entry-cohort labels.
    COPY selected rows into staging.
    COUNT selected source records and staged records.
    VERIFY counts agree under the documented deduplication policy.
    CHECK minimum and maximum selected entry times.
    CHECK null counts in entry, exit, and station fields.
    RECORD unresolved exits separately from missing extraction fields.
    VERIFY station codes are retained without lossy numeric conversion.
    RECORD table schema fingerprint and extraction time.
    IF validation fails:
        LEAVE existing published destination unchanged.
        MARK staging invalid and return failure diagnostics.
    END IF
    IF new_table_name already exists:
        APPLY the declared preserve/version/replace policy.
    END IF
    PUBLISH validated staging under the intended destination identity.
    COMMIT when the database's operation semantics require it.
    RECORD any DDL auto-commit behavior in the receipt.
    RETURN source, destination, bounds, row count, schema version, and validation status.
END PROCEDURE
